tage research may not have been peer reviewed yet.\n\n## Abstract\n\nLet G be a finite simple graph and I(G) denote the corresponding edge ideal. For all $s \\geq 1$, we obtain upper bounds for reg$(I(G)^s)$ for bipartite graphs. We then compare the properties of G and $G'$, where $G'$ is the graph associated with the polarization of the ideal $(I(G)^{s+1} : e_1\\cdots e_s)$, where $e_1,\\ldots e_s$ are edges of G. Using these results, we explicitly compute reg$(I(G)^s)$ for several subclasses of bipartite graphs.\n\n## No file available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest file PDF\n\nE-mail address: jayanav@iitm.ac.in E-mail address: naru@iitm.ac.in E-mail address: selva.y2s@gmail\n\n  * Jan 2004\n  * 2301-2324\n\n  * Xinxian Zheng\n\nXinxian Zheng. Resolutions of facet ideals. Comm. Algebra, 32(6):2301-2324, 2004. E-mail address: jayanav@iitm.ac.in E-mail address: naru@iitm.ac.in E-mail address: selva.y2s@gmail.com Department of Mathematics, Indian Institute of Technology Madras, Chennai, INDIA -60036--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nuntitled (https://ufdcimages.uflib.ufl.edu/UF/00/02/82/95/00683/00005-09-2009.pdf)\nciteturn3search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 17.5 years ago; Proof Deadlines Wednesday at 3:00 pm\n367940\nOF HOMES\nCall Jill at 941-429-3116\nRiverwood is a Gated Community with Golf,\nTennis, Activity Center, State of the Art Fitness\nCenter, Pool, Close to Beaches and Marinas.\nFabulous Lifestyle.\nRiverwood Resales From $175,000-$600,000\nFrom Rt. 41 and 776 in Murdock, go west on 776\nabout 4 miles to entrance\nCome Visit or Call 941-743-9663 or 1-800-874-1869\nCharleston South Condominiums at\n3311 Wood Thrush Dr., Unit 123, PGI\n2nd floor condo, 3 bedrooms and 2 baths. Builders\nclose-out! Sailboat access to Charlotte Harbor with a\ndeeded boat dock. Custom cherry cabinets with\ngranite counters in kitchen and baths. Tray ceilings,\ncrown molding and designer base moldings. Single\ncar garage, paver driveways, walkways and pool deck.\nList Price $239,000. Builder has taken a huge price\nreduction to sell the final units.\nElaine Martin, Real Estate Broker\nFishermen’s Village Realty, LLC.\n941-661-4800\nemail: jilld@sunnewspapers.net\nProof Deadlines Wednesday at 3:00 pm\n367940\n367950\n367975--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInduced matching, ordered matching and Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of bipartite graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.06781)\nciteturn3academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.5 years ago; Title: Induced matching, ordered matching and Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of bipartite graphs ... We also give formulas for the count of connected non-isomorphic spanning subgraphs of the complete bipartite graph K_{m,n} for which indm(G) = ordm(G) = 2, with an explicit expression for the count when m = 2,3,4 and m <= n.\nTitle: Induced matching, ordered matching and Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of bipartite graphs\nAuthors: A. V. Jayanthan, S. A. Seyed Fakhari, I. Swanson, S. Yassemi\nDate: Fri May 10 19:16:31 2024\n\nLet G be a finite simple graph and let indm(G) and ordm(G) denote the induced matching number and the ordered matching number of G, respectively. We characterize all bipartite graphs G with indm(G) = ordm(G). We establish the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of powers of edge ideals and depth of powers of cover ideals for such graphs. We also give formulas for the count of connected non-isomorphic spanning subgraphs of the complete bipartite graph K_{m,n} for which indm(G) = ordm(G) = 2, with an explicit expression for the count when m = 2,3,4 and m <= n.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nREGULARITY OF POWERS OF BIPARTITE GRAPHS | Bulletin of the Australian Mathematical Society | Cambridge Core (https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/bulletin-of-the-australian-mathematical-society/article/abs/regularity-of-powers-of-bipartite-graphs/B3AC32380FCA256B8B1AC3E085144394)\nciteturn3search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.1 years ago; Crawled: last week; For a simple bipartite graph G, we give an upper bound for the regularity of powers of the edge ideal Image in terms of its vertex domination number. ... Bıyıkoğlu, T. and Civan, Y., ‘Projective dimension of (hyper)graphs and the Castelnuovo–Mumford regularity of bipartite graphs’, Preprint, 2016, arXiv:1605.02956.\n\n# REGULARITY OF POWERS OF BIPARTITE GRAPHS\n\nPart of: Algebraic combinatorics Commutative algebra: Homological methods Theory of modules and ideals\n\nPublished online by Cambridge University Press:  19 September 2022\n\nAJAY KUMAR  and\n\nRAJIV KUMAR\n\nAJAY KUMAR*\n    Affiliation:\n\nDepartment of Mathematics, Indian Institute of Technology Jammu, Jammu, India\n\nRAJIV KUMAR\n    Affiliation:\n\nDepartment of Mathematics, Indian Institute of Technology Jammu, Jammu, India e-mail: gargrajiv00@gmail.com\n\n*\n    \n\ne-mail: ajay.kumar@iitjammu.ac.in\n\n## Abstract\n\nFor a simple bipartite graph G, we give an upper bound for the regularity of powers of the edge ideal Image in terms of its vertex domination number. Consequently, we explicitly compute the regularity of powers of the edge ideal of a bipartite Kneser graph. Further, we compute the induced matching number of a bipartite Kneser graph.\n\n* * *\n\n## Keywords\n\nregularitybipartite Kneser graphedge idealvertex domination number\n\n* * *\n\n## MSC classification\n\nPrimary: 05E40: Combinatorial aspects of commutative algebra\n\nSecondary: 13C14: Cohen-Macaulay modules 13D02: Syzygies, resolutions, complexes\n\nType\n    Research Article\n\nInformation\n    \n\nBulletin of the Australian Mathematical Society , Volume 107 , Issue 1 , February 2023 , pp. 1 - 9\n\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.1017/S0004972722000855 [Opens in a new window]\n\nCopyright\n    \n\n© The Author(s), 2022. Published by Cambridge University Press on behalf of Australian Mathematical Publishing Association Inc.\n\n## References\n\n[1]\n\nAlilooee, A. and Banerjee, A., ‘Powers of edge ideals of regularity three bipartite graphs’, J. Commut. Algebra 9(4) (2017), 441–454.CrossRefGoogle Scholar\n\n[2]\n\nBanerjee, A., ‘The regularity of powers of edge ideals’, J. Algebraic Combin. 41(2) (2015), 303–321.CrossRefGoogle Scholar\n\n[3]\n\nBeyarslan, S., Hà, H. T. and Trung, T. N., ‘Regularity of powers of forests and cycles’, J. Algebraic Combin. 42(4) (2015), 1077–1095.CrossRefGoogle Scholar\n\n[4]\n\nBıyıkoğlu, T. and Civan, Y., ‘Projective dimension of (hyper)graphs and the Castelnuovo–Mumford regularity of bipartite graphs’, Preprint, 2016, arXiv:1605.02956.Google Scholar\n\n[5]\n\nCutkosky, S. D., Herzog, J. and Trung, N. V., ‘Asymptotic behaviour of the Castelnuovo–Mumford regularity, Compos. Math. 118(3) (1999), 243–261.CrossRefGoogle Scholar\n\n[6]\n\nFrankl, P., ‘An extremal problem for two families of sets’, European J. Combin. 3(2) (1982), 125–127.CrossRefGoogle Scholar\n\n[7]\n\nHerzog, J. and Hibi, T., ‘An upper bound for the regularity of powers of edge ideals’, Math. Scand. 126(2) (2020), 165–169.【--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nREGULARITY OF POWERS OF BIPARTITE GRAPHS (https://home.iitm.ac.in/naru/mypapers/monomials.pdf)\nciteturn3search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; REGULARITY OF POWERS OF BIPARTITE GRAPHS ... the properties of G and G′, where G′ is the graph associated with the polarization of the ... active research on bounding the homological invariants of edge ideals in terms of the com- ... arXiv:1609.01402v1  [math.AC]  6 Sep 2016\nREGULARITY OF POWERS OF BIPARTITE GRAPHS\nA. V. JAYANTHAN, N. NARAYANAN, AND S. SELVARAJA\nAbstract. Let G be a ﬁnite simple graph and I(G) denote the corresponding edge ideal.\nFor all s ≥1, we obtain upper bounds for reg(I(G)s) for bipartite graphs. We then compare\nthe properties of G and G′, where G′ is the graph associated with the polarization of the\nideal (I(G)s+1 : e1 · · · es), where e1, . . . es are edges of G. Using these results, we explicitly\ncompute reg(I(G)s) for several subclasses of bipartite graphs.\n1. Introduction\nLet G = (V (G), E(G)) denote a ﬁnite simple undirected graph with vertices V (G) =\n{x1, . . . , xn} and edge set E(G). By identifying the vertices with the variables in the poly-\nnomial ring k[x1, . . . , xn], where k is a ﬁeld, we can associate to each graph G a monomial\nideal I(G) generated by the set {xixj | {xi, xj} ∈E(G)}. The ideal I(G) is called the edge\nideal of G. This notion was introduced by Villarreal in [29]. Since then, the researchers\nhave been investigating the connection between the combinatorial properties of the graphs\nand the algebraic properties of the corresponding edge ideals. In particular, there have been\nactive research on bounding the homological invariants of edge ideals in terms of the com-\nbinatorial invariants of the associated graphs, see for example [3], [10], [12], [15], [17], [19],\n[22], [23], [26], [28], [32], [33]. In this article, we study the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity\nof powers of edge ideals of bipartite graphs. For a homogeneous ideal I, we denote by reg(I),\nthe Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity, henceforth called regularity, of I.\nIt was proved by Cutkosky, Herzog and Trung, [9], and independently by Kodiyalam [20],\nthat for a homogeneous ideal I in a polynomial ring, reg(Is) is a linear function for s ≫0,\ni.e., there exist integers a, b, s0 such that\nreg(Is) = as + b for all s ≥s0.\narXiv:1609.01402v1  [math.AC]  6 Sep 2016\nIt is known that a is bounded above by the maximum of degree of elements in a minimal\ngenerating set of I. But a general bound for b as well as s0 is unknown. In this paper, we\nconsider I = I(G), the edge ideal of G. In this case, there exist integers b and s0 such that\nreg(Is) = 2s + b for all s ≥s0. Our objective in this paper is to ﬁnd b and s0 in terms of\ncombinatorial invariants of the graph G. We refer the reader to [5] for a review of results in\nthe literature which identify classes of edge ideals for which b and s0 are explicitly computed.\nIt is known that for any graph G,\nν(G) + 1 ≤reg(I(G)) ≤co-chord(G) + 1,\n(1.1)\nwhere ν(G) denote the induced matching number of G and co-chord(G) denote the co-chordal\ncover number of G. The lower bound was proved by Katzman, [18] and the upper bound\nwas proved by Woodroofe, [32]. Beyarslan, H`a and Trung proved that for any graph G and\ns ≥1, 2s + ν(G) −1 ≤reg(I(G))s, [5]. They also proved that the equality holds for edge\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIN THE COURT OF COMMON PLEAS, FRANKLIN COUNTY, OHIO (https://dam.assets.ohio.gov/image/upload/insurance.ohio.gov/liq/documents/22_20100927_MotionForOrderApprovingFinalClaimsReport.pdf)\nciteturn3search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Proof of Claims - Class 05 ... 367940\n38\nPage\n9/27/10\n10:38:01\nOAY05\nOSOETVAJ;.P1\nDayMed - Class 5 Final Distribution -ElxhibitA\nProof of Claims - Class 05\nDetermined Value Distribution Report\nDistribution percentage\n75.1260%\nCheck Amount\nLess: Prevpayments/Allow\nTotal Distribution Payment\n-------~--~--~--------~-~-----------------------------\n---------------------\nDetermined value\nDistribution\nPayee/Address\nClaim#\nLiq#/seq#\n00367800\n01\n367800\n135.00\n75.1260%\n101.42\n.00\n101.42\n00367838\n01\n367838\n.00\"\"\n75.1260%\n.00\n.00\n.00\n00367844\n01\n367844\n1,801.52\n75.1260%\n1,353.41\n.00\n1,353.41\n00367852\n01\n367852\n.00\n75.1260%\n.00\n.00\n.00\n00367860\n01\n367860\n263,00\n75.1260%\n197.58\n,00\n197.58\n00367877\n01\n367877\n264.00\n75.1260%\n198.33\n.00\n198.33\n75.1260%\n.00\n.00\n.00\n.00\n367882\n00367882\n01\n350.64\n.00\n263.42\n263.42\n75.1260%\n00367909\n01\n367909\n.00\n.00\n.00\n75.1260%\n.00\n367924\n00367924\n01\n75.1260%\n.00\n.00\n.0